        "narrative": "<p>Canoe Lake is generally not known as a destination lake for BWCAW fishing trips, and the results of the 1999 survey bear this out.  Catches for all species were below average for lakes of this class.  Very few walleye were present, and no northern pike or smallmouth bass were taken (although they may have been present in small numbers).  Forage for game fish was very limited; the yellow perch catch was low, and no minnows were taken in minnow traps set along the shore.</p>",
